From: u9340abd652779041 at groups.google.com (Theo Bromine)
Date: Fri, 18 Jan 2019 15:01:56 +0000
Subject: Differential methylation analysis for paired patiend data
Message-ID: <CP3nR6iLMR8.4v_G9Zo7AwAJ@methylkit-discussion.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/methylkit_discussion/c/CP3nR6iLMR8/m/4v_G9Zo7AwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi, I have a set of RRBS data for which I have each patient analysed before and after treatment. I would like to perform differential analysis for paired data so each patient is matched before and after. Is there a way to do this using methylkit? If not do you know any good tool can do it smoothly?
Thanks!

From uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com  Sun Jan 20 15:40:57 2019
From: uab8277113f65c05e at groups.google.com (Altuna Akalin)
